# Implementation Plan - Chat Real-time Updates

The customer chat interface currently does not update automatically when new messages arrive. This is because the message list is rendered once on the server and never refreshed on the client. To fix this, I will implement a polling mechanism to periodically fetch new messages.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> I will be using **Polling** (every 3 seconds) to fetch new messages. This is a simple and robust solution for Vercel deployments where long-running connections (Websockets) can be tricky without external services like Pusher or Supabase Realtime.

## Proposed Changes

### Chat Components

#### [MODIFY] [message-list.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx)
- Add a polling mechanism using `useEffect` and `setInterval`.
- Call the [getMessages](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/chat.actions.ts#40-59) Server Action to fetch the latest messages.
- Update the message list state when new messages arrive.
- Ensure the scroll position is handled correctly (only scroll to bottom if already at bottom or new message is from self).

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/(dashboard)/chat/[customerId]/page.tsx)
- Pass the `customerId` to [MessageList](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#33-61) explicitly.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  Open the Chat page for a specific customer.
2.  Send a message from the LINE app (as the customer) to the LINE OA.
3.  Observe that the message appears in the Admin Panel chat window within 3-4 seconds without refreshing the page.
4.  Send a message from the Admin Panel.
5.  Observe it appears immediately.
